:\"payments-worker\",\"severity\":\"SEV2\",\"summary\":\"Since this morning's deploy of v3.4.0, payments-worker has been unhealthy with an elevated error rate (18%) across all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Rolled back all production regions to the most recent healthy release, v3.3.0. Monitoring for recovery.\",\"title\":\"payments-worker unhealthy after v3.4.0 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v3.3.0\"}", "name": "create_incident"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "Let me verify the service has recovered.", "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150ba3a1d77ac87580ae9", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-worker\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "stop", "content": "Done. Here's a summary of what happened:\n\n**Issue:** The errors traced to **payments-worker**, which had been unhealthy since this morning's deploy of v3.4.0 (18% error rate across us-east, us-west, and eu-west).\n\n**Actions taken:**\n1. **Rollback** \u2014 Rolled payments-worker back to **v3.3.0**, its most recent release that was healthy in production, across all production regions.\n2. **Incident** \u2014 Opened **SEV2 incident INC-0001**, which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n**Verification:** payments-worker is now healthy again on v3.3.0, with the error rate down to 0.2% (from 18%).\n\nNote: My first rollback attempt targeted \"payments-api\" (which was also showing degradation), but the approver corrected that the actual problem was in payments-worker, so the rollback was redirected accordingly. If you'd like the payments-api degradation investigated separately, I can open an incident for it.", "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": []}]}